 {
  "src": "HN",
  "title": "Ask HN: If the models are so good, why doesn't OpenAI just start 100 companies?",
  "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997",
  "discuss": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997",
  "score": 206,
  "comments": 201,
  "age_h": 14.8,
  "text": "Title is a bit of an exaggeration but the question is more: if the frontier models are so good, why even sell them as your primary money maker?<p>Couldn&#x27;t OpenAI or Anthropic make a lot more money by just starting companies themselves that leverage the models and building their own products?<p>Is selling tokens really the best strategy?<p>Especially with commodification and prices declining wouldn&#x27;t that indicate there is more money to be made on the application-side of the models rather than the utility side"
